{"id":"94bd1a46-4cdf-4b34-aab4-8bb98797b45d","title":"12SEN_Cycle5","fetched":"2026-10-23T23:58:44.276Z","questions":[{"id":"1faa113f-233e-4cbc-99d5-906c2f150d0f","title":"Social Issues / Approaches / Implementation Methods (Q21, 2018 HSC Exam SDD)","isPublished":true,"publishDate":"2025-05-09T04:09:21.165Z","syllabusId":"d1a54432-597e-4e3c-a5c6-ad7a134726e4","stimulusContentItemCollection":{"id":"d19feeaf-ab48-4875-a1d2-1139b8c10ecb","items":[{"id":"d837717e-18f0-4c31-8b60-d3286b697458","updatedDate":"2025-04-29T03:57:29.400Z","files":null,"type":"RICH_TEXT","text":"<p>A new smartphone app is to be developed for registered users to hire cars. Registered&nbsp;users can use the app to find the location of available cars, unlock them for use and&nbsp;lock them after use. The bank account of the user is debited automatically based on&nbsp;the time for which the car was used. The app will also be continually upgraded to&nbsp;enhance user experience.</p>"}],"itemIdOrder":["d837717e-18f0-4c31-8b60-d3286b697458"]},"publisher":null,"dynamicFields":null,"copyrightText":"HSC 2018","visibility":"PUBLIC","school":{"id":"7572b03a-1507-4309-950e-2a286bdcf0a4","name":"The King's School, Parramatta"},"systemId":null,"system":null,"isPublisherLocked":false,"parts":[{"id":"6f701a3c-2f5d-4c75-8c25-13a48c9cbe8c","displayIndex":0,"title":"Part A","metadata":{"id":"e2849890-8283-4cb6-a1ac-ced1ae5ec59b","mark":3,"syllabus":{"id":"d1a54432-597e-4e3c-a5c6-ad7a134726e4","title":"Software Engineering","description":"Software Engineering Stage 6 Syllabus 2022","gradeFrom":12,"gradeTo":12,"coverageLabel":null,"curriculumCode":null,"curriculumVersion":null,"gradingScaleName":null,"publishedYear":null,"publishedDate":null},"band":null,"outcomeIds":["880073ce-5d0d-42bf-8c8c-3fc3d64646df"],"topicIds":["36d3695c-0bfb-42fc-960e-59e5ff103fb7","a45d4626-6ce7-44bc-b6a2-d0fcaeea9412"],"subtopicIds":["542010fc-1f65-4619-b24f-fc6b3aa7fc0c","f688e948-0754-41f7-8f81-79e0c3a0e473"],"subtopicItemIds":["218361aa-1cb5-4b5b-b3c3-ecbb658a7962","35d54351-8e4c-4791-a5f5-9a65d4385003"],"bandIds":["b87d71ee-5ae9-43f7-a1f5-feec3f1db295"]},"content":{"id":"4cb31583-fa64-4fd3-9966-ce9bc2a5e97b","contentItemCollection":{"id":"b263828f-0cc8-4034-bbf2-1d677ead45f6","items":[{"id":"d4ff1c67-3865-466c-804a-112fb2851268","updatedDate":"2025-05-09T04:09:22.606Z","files":null,"type":"RICH_TEXT","text":"<p>Outline the social and ethical issues that the developer needs to take into account&nbsp;when developing this app</p>"}],"itemIdOrder":["d4ff1c67-3865-466c-804a-112fb2851268"]},"contentItemMetadata":null},"answer":{"id":"68605307-fca7-4347-b5a3-01612495f4f1","parameters":{"version":0,"type":"SHORT","extendedView":true,"settings":{"version":0,"wordLimit":false,"wordCount":null,"exactValue":false,"richText":true,"imageUpload":false,"equationEditor":false,"calculatorInterface":false},"correctValues":null},"files":null},"markingCriteriaContentItem":{"id":"e4b3ba3b-0705-4c01-bdbf-1847861cc8d8","updatedDate":"2026-10-20T09:43:19.218Z","files":null,"type":"MARKING_CRITERIA","criteria":[{"criterion":"<p>Outlines social and ethical issues with reference to this system</p>","point":"<p>3</p>"},{"criterion":"<p>Outlines one social ethical issue with reference to this system</p>","point":"<p>2</p>"},{"criterion":"<p>Identifies a social or ethical issue</p>","point":"1"}]},"markingRubricContentItem":null,"markingGuidanceContentItem":null,"sampleAnswerContentItem":{"id":"e5bd2f52-84e9-48a1-92e8-0417bf5ed6b4","updatedDate":"2025-05-09T04:09:22.775Z","files":null,"type":"RICH_TEXT","text":"<p>It is possible to store details of every trip made by each user. This could be used by those&nbsp;wanting to track the routes taken eg employers, stalkers, potential advertisers.&nbsp;Those not wanting to provide bank account details or without a smartphone or connectivity,&nbsp;can&rsquo;t hire the cars.</p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Answers could include:&nbsp;</strong></span></p>\n<p>Bank account details need to be stored securely</p>"}},{"id":"fac75da6-8e0b-41c1-9812-bdf86fc2d139","displayIndex":1,"title":"Part B","metadata":{"id":"70812562-90ea-46d5-8541-3f5fe6e67fd5","mark":3,"syllabus":{"id":"d1a54432-597e-4e3c-a5c6-ad7a134726e4","title":"Software Engineering","description":"Software Engineering Stage 6 Syllabus 2022","gradeFrom":12,"gradeTo":12,"coverageLabel":null,"curriculumCode":null,"curriculumVersion":null,"gradingScaleName":null,"publishedYear":null,"publishedDate":null},"band":null,"outcomeIds":["10d250f1-b45a-44c3-96b5-942f2657212e"],"topicIds":["36d3695c-0bfb-42fc-960e-59e5ff103fb7"],"subtopicIds":["579e1577-2ec7-4c61-bd31-7f401d3edb66"],"subtopicItemIds":["f71e6901-4f93-4a2a-b242-8b941d5b3c9a"],"bandIds":["b87d71ee-5ae9-43f7-a1f5-feec3f1db295"]},"content":{"id":"2738fc68-c439-4d91-8cb6-9f1102c0d41d","contentItemCollection":{"id":"8d1fa9c2-fc9a-4f85-8356-d8a7529dcbce","items":[{"id":"7d6256f6-45a8-474b-994f-22d2bf9ca2f3","updatedDate":"2025-04-29T03:59:41.007Z","files":null,"type":"RICH_TEXT","text":"<p>Justify an appropriate software development approach for the smartphone app.</p>"}],"itemIdOrder":["7d6256f6-45a8-474b-994f-22d2bf9ca2f3"]},"contentItemMetadata":null},"answer":{"id":"20ca0d9b-cf2d-49e6-8abe-119b8c346d17","parameters":{"version":0,"type":"SHORT","extendedView":true,"settings":{"version":0,"wordLimit":false,"wordCount":null,"exactValue":false,"richText":true,"imageUpload":false,"equationEditor":false,"calculatorInterface":false},"correctValues":null},"files":null},"markingCriteriaContentItem":{"id":"0b3afc36-c25a-4ac6-9bc0-cc20d5199519","updatedDate":"2025-05-09T03:53:33.341Z","files":null,"type":"MARKING_CRITERIA","criteria":[{"criterion":"<p>Identifies an appropriate development approach and provides thorough&nbsp;justification</p>","point":"3"},{"criterion":"<p>Identifies an appropriate development approach with some justification</p>","point":"2"},{"criterion":"<p>Identifies a development approach</p>","point":"1"}]},"markingRubricContentItem":null,"markingGuidanceContentItem":null,"sampleAnswerContentItem":{"id":"4a050878-209d-49e0-8111-1ec9e0a31c04","updatedDate":"2025-04-29T04:08:00.772Z","files":null,"type":"RICH_TEXT","text":"<p>The flexible agile approach is best suited as it allows for new versions to be delivered&nbsp;quickly, enabling the incorporation of new features in a short timeframe, based on user&nbsp;feedback. Because the car share application is relatively small and online, users will easily&nbsp;accept new features as they are identified and implemented. The users will appreciate the&nbsp;responsiveness of the app developers to their feedback</p>"}},{"id":"532b3dbd-e2be-4f72-a1f5-405f349c1e90","displayIndex":2,"title":"Part C","metadata":{"id":"58a35d3d-76d8-44b4-a591-d47bf364343e","mark":3,"syllabus":{"id":"d1a54432-597e-4e3c-a5c6-ad7a134726e4","title":"Software Engineering","description":"Software Engineering Stage 6 Syllabus 2022","gradeFrom":12,"gradeTo":12,"coverageLabel":null,"curriculumCode":null,"curriculumVersion":null,"gradingScaleName":null,"publishedYear":null,"publishedDate":null},"band":null,"outcomeIds":["10d250f1-b45a-44c3-96b5-942f2657212e","72cda872-f70a-431a-a485-a9d3f0712ea1"],"topicIds":["36d3695c-0bfb-42fc-960e-59e5ff103fb7"],"subtopicIds":["1c979db8-b3ef-4a1a-bcaa-f5ebe8268617"],"subtopicItemIds":["30c27bb1-a41d-4d43-bea6-19ed73405b66"],"bandIds":["b87d71ee-5ae9-43f7-a1f5-feec3f1db295"]},"content":{"id":"a6ad5098-53ee-4999-a6cb-6bd9dc788cc0","contentItemCollection":{"id":"61b419c3-f8aa-4181-91fb-8ce6b196b665","items":[{"id":"74948d62-3b57-4320-b681-3b72f2f90ccf","updatedDate":"2025-05-09T03:53:49.252Z","files":null,"type":"RICH_TEXT","text":"<p>Justify a suitable installation method for the smartphone app.</p>"}],"itemIdOrder":["74948d62-3b57-4320-b681-3b72f2f90ccf"]},"contentItemMetadata":null},"answer":{"id":"bae1bdb4-27af-426e-a508-10175946b2c2","parameters":{"version":0,"type":"SHORT","extendedView":true,"settings":{"version":0,"wordLimit":false,"wordCount":null,"exactValue":false,"richText":true,"imageUpload":false,"equationEditor":false,"calculatorInterface":false},"correctValues":null},"files":null},"markingCriteriaContentItem":{"id":"3298c310-2841-44d1-97ca-924db9128b27","updatedDate":"2025-05-09T03:53:41.375Z","files":null,"type":"MARKING_CRITERIA","criteria":[{"criterion":"<p>Identifies a suitable installation method and provides thorough justification</p>","point":"<p>3</p>"},{"criterion":"<p>Identifies a suitable installation method and provides some justification</p>","point":"<p>2</p>"},{"criterion":"<p>Identifies an installation method</p>","point":"1"}]},"markingRubricContentItem":null,"markingGuidanceContentItem":null,"sampleAnswerContentItem":{"id":"97d433aa-2f1c-41a8-ab6e-79353508ac32","updatedDate":"2025-05-09T03:53:49.350Z","files":null,"type":"RICH_TEXT","text":"<p>Pilot.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The developers could select a limited area eg a suburb, with representative car hirers to test the system before rolling it out over the whole country/city. Feedback from the users can be used to identify issues and allow appropriate modifications to be made. In this way the impact of any issues can be minimised and resolved before the larger rollout</p>"}}]}],"answers":[{"partId":"6f701a3c-2f5d-4c75-8c25-13a48c9cbe8c","studentId":"0071efd7-8807-43a2-96e7-9085b48c8632","examAnswerSheetItem":null,"mark":null,"markingSessionMarkingItemList":[]},{"partId":"fac75da6-8e0b-41c1-9812-bdf86fc2d139","studentId":"0071efd7-8807-43a2-96e7-9085b48c8632","examAnswerSheetItem":null,"mark":null,"markingSessionMarkingItemList":[]},{"partId":"532b3dbd-e2be-4f72-a1f5-405f349c1e90","studentId":"0071efd7-8807-43a2-96e7-9085b48c8632","examAnswerSheetItem":null,"mark":null,"markingSessionMarkingItemList":[]}],"state":{"isFinished":true,"dynamicFieldSeed":null,"markerUserList":[{"id":"4e096daa-d1c7-47e9-9c7b-c1adaf476532","firstName":"TKS","lastName":"CST"}],"examTitle":"12SEN_Cycle5"}}